 "id": "story-4-reviews-given",
 "name": "Story 4: reviewing teammates' PRs",
 "description": "Teammates ask me for reviews; some PRs carry a real defect, fewer as the team's skill rises. An agent writes a pre-read brief from its map of the codebase, which it improves with every review. I review: whether I catch a defect depends on the brief and how long my queue is. Caught defects teach authors and build my reputation, which brings more requests; missed ones land and come back as bugs. Reviews given build goodwill (which, in the desk model, speeds reviews of my own PRs); nitpicks spend it. Time unit: a working hour; horizon 26 weeks.",
